'''Michael Snyder''' is an actor who played different characters in two {{Star Trek films}} and two episodes of {{s|TNG}}. He is one of 32 actors who have played in both {{s|TOS}} (or one of its movies) and one of the spin-off series. Snyder filmed his scenes for the episode "The Perfect Mate" between Tuesday {{d|18|February|1992}} and Thursday {{d|20|February|1992}} on [[Paramount Stage 8]] and [[Paramount Stage 9|9]].

Besides his ''Star Trek'' appearances he played a video camera assistant in {{wt|Funny About Love}} (1990), which was directed by [[Leonard Nimoy]] and featured ''Trek'' guest stars [[Andrew Hill Newman]], [[Paul Collins]], [[Michael Bofshever]], [[Celeste Yarnall]], and stunt coordinator [[Greg Barnett]].

Michael Snyder also worked opposite Leonard Nimoy in the original Broadway Production of ''Equus''.

