'''Jerry Hardin''' {{born|20|November|1929}} is an actor who played [[Radue]] in the {{s|TNG}} [[TNG Season 1|first season]] episode {{e|When The Bough Breaks}}, [[Samuel Clemens]] in the [[TNG Season 5|fifth]] and [[TNG Season 6|sixth season]] episodes {{e|Time's Arrow}} and {{e|Time's Arrow, Part II}}, and [[Neria]] in the {{s|VOY}} [[VOY Season 1|first season]] episode {{e|Emanations}}.

Elsewhere in the sci-fi genre, Hardin is well-known for his portrayal of the informant Deep Throat beginning in the first season of ''[[The X-Files]]'', as well as his role as the unnamed attorney in {{wt|Big Trouble in Little China}} (1986, starring [[Kim Cattrall]]). He had a bit part in {{wt|Mitchell (film)|Mitchell}} (1975, with [[Robert Phillips]]). He also had a small role in the 1981 ''Star Wars Radio Drama'' as the voices of additional characters.

He has made guest appearances in {{wt|Ironside (1967 TV series)|Ironside}} (starring [[Barbara Anderson]]), {{wt|Starsky & Hutch}} (1977, starring [[David Soul]], with [[Eugene Roche]]), {{wt|The Rockford Files}}, {{wt|Little House on the Prairie (TV series)|Little House on the Prairie}}, {{wt|The Twilight Zone (1985 TV series)|The Twilight Zone}} (with [[Andrew J. Robinson]], [[Louis Giambalvo]], [[Mark L. Taylor]] and [[David Sage]]), {{wt|Dallas (TV series)|Dallas}} (starring [[Susan Howard]], with [[William Smithers]]), {{wt|Knots Landing}}, {{wt|Quantum Leap (1989 TV series)|Quantum Leap}} (1992, starring and directed by [[Scott Bakula]], co-starring [[Dean Stockwell]], with [[Alan Oppenheimer]] and [[Barbara J. Tarbuck]]), {{wt|Lois & Clark: The New Adventures of Superman}} (starring [[Teri Hatcher]], [[K Callan]] and [[Tracy Scoggins]]), {{wt|Dr. Quinn, Medicine Woman}} {{wt|Murder, She Wrote}}, {{wt|Melrose Place}}, {{wt|Sliders (TV series)|Sliders}} (1999, starring [[Jerry O'Connell]], with [[Ken Jenkins]] and [[Kristanna S. Loken]]) and ''The Middle''.

