'''Anne Haney''' {{born|4|March|1934|died|26|May|2001}}<sup>{{el|findagrave.com/memorial/6809320}}</sup> was the actress who played [[Rishon Uxbridge]] in the {{s|TNG}} [[TNG Season 3|third season]] episode {{e|The Survivors}} and [[Els Renora]] in the {{s|DS9}} [[DS9 Season 1|first season]] episode {{e|Dax}}.

Haney was a regular on {{wt|Mama's Family}} from 1986 through 1989, and had a recurring role as Judge Marilyn Travelini on {{wt|L.A. Law}} from 1986 through 1994. She also appeared in two episodes of {{wt|Quantum Leap (1989 TV series)|Quantum Leap}}, starring [[Scott Bakula]] and [[Dean Stockwell]], former with [[Parley Baer]] and the latter with [[Hal Landon, Jr.]] and [[Patrick Massett]]. She also appeared with [[Andrew Robinson]] in the 1981 failed television pilot, ''Big Bend Country'' which was directed by [[Ralph Senensky]].

Her feature film credits include ''K-9000'' (1991; with [[Judson Scott]], [[David Renan]], [[Ted Barba]], [[James H. Burk]], [[Kenny Endoso]], [[Jeff Imada]], [[Dave Perna]], and [[Nicholas Shaffer]], and with stunts by [[Greg Barnett]] and [[Lane Leavitt]]), {{wt|Mrs. Doubtfire}} (1993, starring [[Robin Williams]] and [[Pierce Brosnan]], with [[William Newman]]), {{wt|The American President}} (1995), and {{wt|Liar Liar}} (1997, featuring [[Mitchell Ryan]], [[Ernest Perry, Jr.]], and [[Eric Pierpoint]]. She co-starred in {{wt|Roses Are for the Rich}} (1987, featuring {{s|VOY}} stars [[Kate Mulgrew]] and [[Robert Picardo]]). She later appeared in {{wt|Psycho (1998 film)|Psycho}} (1998, featuring [[Ken Jenkins]] and [[Roy Brocksmith]]). 

She also guest-starred in an episode of {{wt|The Golden Girls}} (1992, with [[Robert Picardo]] and [[Bill Quinn]]). 

At the age of 67, Haney died of congestive heart failure at her home in Studio City, Los Angeles, California. {{el|sfgate.com/news/article/Anne-Haney-67-character-actress-in-films-TV-2912764.php}}

