'''Scott Thomson''' {{born|29|October|1957}}{{incite|date=March 2023}} is the actor who portrayed [[Goss]] in the {{s|TNG}} [[TNG Season 3|third season]] episode {{e|The Price}}.

His first feature film was {{wt|Smokey and the Bandit}} (1977, with [[Paul Williams]] and [[Paul Sorensen]]. Later he appeared in {{wt|Parasite (1982 film)|Parasite}} (1982, with [[Tom Villard]]). Thomson's well known appearance came in {{wt|Fast Times at Ridgemont High}} (1982, with [[Ray Walston]], [[Vincent Schiavelli]], and [[Hallie Todd]]) and he starred in ''Frightmare'' (1983, with [[Jeffrey Combs]]), {{wt|Johnny Dangerously}} (1984, with Ray Walston, [[Joe Piscopo]], and Vincent Schiavelli), and {{wt|Ghoulies}} (1985).

Thomson played Chad Copeland in {{wt|Police Academy}} (1984, with [[David Graf]] and [[Kim Cattrall]]), {{wt|Police Academy 3: Back in Training}} (1986, with David Graf, [[Arthur Batanides]], and [[Brian Tochi]]) and {{wt|Police Academy 4: Citizens on Patrol}} (1987, with David Graf, Brian Tochi and [[Carolyn Scott]]).

Other films include {{wt|The Couch Trip}} (1988, with [[Michael Ensign]], [[Don Stark]], and [[John Mahon]]), {{wt|Casual Sex?}} (1988, starring [[Lea Thompson]], with [[Dan Woren]], [[Leslie Morris]], [[Tina Lifford]], [[Barbara Harris]], [[David McCharen]], and [[Gary Schwartz]]), {{wt|Day One (1989 film)|Day One}} (1989, with [[David Ogden Stiers]] and [[Alan Scarfe]]), {{wt|Jack the Bear}} (1993, with [[Stefan Gierasch]], [[Bert Remsen]], [[Lorinne Vozoff]], [[Kevin McDermott]], and [[Kelly Connell]]), {{wt|Mr. Jones (1993 film)|Mr. Jones}} (1993, with [[Lauren Tom]], [[Thomas Kopache]], [[Peter Vogt]], [[Irene Tsu]], [[Albert Henderson]], and [[John Durbin]]), {{wt|My Summer Story}} (1994, with [[Roy Brocksmith]], [[Wayne Grace]], and [[Frank Collison]]), {{wt|Twister (1996 film)|Twister}} (1996, with [[Alan Ruck]], [[Sean Whalen]], [[Zach Grenier]], [[Patrick Fischler]], [[Anthony Rapp]], [[Richard Lineback]], and [[Bruce Wright]]), {{wt|Blast from the Past (film)|Blast from the Past}} (1999, with [[Ryan Sparks]], [[Richard Gilbert-Hill]], and [[Annie O'Donnell]]), {{wt|Loser (2000 film)|Loser}} (2000, with [[Jimmi Simpson]], [[Andy Dick]], [[Robert Miano]], and [[Andrea Martin]]), [[Jonathan Frakes]]' {{wt|Clockstoppers}} (2002, starring [[Ken Jenkins]], [[Jenette Goldstein]], [[Gina Hecht]], [[Jeff Ricketts]], and [[Billy Mayo]]), and ''Assumption'' (2006).

Thomson has appeared in television series such as {{wt|The Greatest American Hero}} (1981), {{wt|T. J. Hooker}} (1982, starring [[William Shatner]], with [[Richard Herd]] and directed by [[Cliff Bole]]), {{wt|Hunter (1984 American TV series)|Hunter}} (1989, starring [[Charles Hallahan]], with [[Fionnula Flanagan]], [[Alan Scarfe]], and [[Nicholas Guest]]), ''Parker Lewis Can't Lose'' (1990, with [[Sherman Howard]] and [[Clyde Kusatsu]]), ''The Cosby Mysteries'' (1994, with [[Zach Grenier]]), {{wt|Big Love}} (2009, with [[Robert Beltran]], [[Charles Esten]], [[Miriam Flynn]], [[Noa Tishby]], and [[Time Winters]]), and {{wt|Ghost Whisperer}} (2009, with [[Kelli Kirkland]]).

He later had a guest part in {{wt|True Blood}} (2010, with [[Kristin Bauer]] and [[Gregg Daniel]]) and appeared in the comedy ''Vamps'' (2011, with [[Wallace Shawn]] and [[Malcolm McDowell]]) and {{wt|Night of the Living Dead 3D: Re-Animation}} (2012, with [[Jeffrey Combs]] and [[Rhonda Aldrich]]).

