'''Galyn Görg''' {{born|15|July|1964|died|14|July|2020}} was an actress, dancer, and choreographer who appeared as [[Korena]] in the {{s|DS9}} [[DS9 Season 4|fourth season]] episode {{e|The Visitor}} and {{dis|Nori|Ilari}} in the {{s|VOY}} [[VOY Season 3|third season]] episode {{e|Warlord}} for which she filmed her scenes between Friday {{d|30|August|1996}} and Monday {{d|9|September|1996}} on [[Paramount Stage 8]], [[Paramount Stage 9|9]], and [[Paramount Stage 16|16]]. Her costume from this episode was later worn by an [[Unimatrix Zero members 001|unknown actress]] in the [[VOY Season 7|seventh season]] episode {{e|Unimatrix Zero, Part II}} and sold off on the [[It's A Wrap! sale and auction]] on eBay. {{stala|10226}}

Görg is probably best known for her recurring role as Nancy O'Reilly in three second season episodes of {{wt|Twin Peaks}} (1990, with [[Mädchen Amick]], [[Richard Beymer]], [[Ray Wise]], [[Sheryl Lee]], [[Miguel Ferrer]], [[Wendy Robie]], [[Catherine Coulson]], [[Carel Struycken]] and [[David L. Lander]]), her starring role as Lt. Leora Maxwell in {{wt|M.A.N.T.I.S.}} (1994-95, co-starring [[Gary Graham]]), and her guest roles in episodes of {{wt|Xena: Warrior Princess}} (1996), {{wt|Hercules: The Legendary Journeys}} (1996, directed by [[Anson Williams]]), and ''[[Stargate SG-1]]'' (1997, starring [[Richard Dean Anderson]] and [[Michael Shanks]], with [[Vincent Hammond]]).

Other television shows she guest starred on include {{wt|Fame (1982) TV series)|Fame}} (1984, with [[Page Leong]]), {{wt|The A-Team}} (1985, starring [[Dwight Schultz]], with [[Jimmie F. Skaggs]]), {{wt|The Fresh Prince of Bel-Air}} (1996, with [[James Avery]] and [[Daniel Riordan]]), {{wt|Crossing Jordan}} (2001, starring Miguel Ferrer, with [[Marlene Forte]], [[Tom McCleister]], [[Nan Martin]], [[Greg Bronson]] and [[Edward Conna]]), {{wt|CSI: Miami}} (2004, with [[David Lee Smith]], [[Holmes R. Osborne]], [[Gary Wayton]] and [[Richard Ortega-Miro]]), [[J.J. Abrams]]' and [[Damon Lindelof]]'s {{wt|Lost (TV series)|Lost}} (2008, starring [[Naveen Andrews]] and [[Terry O'Quinn]]), and {{wt|Parks and Recreation}} (2015, with [[Adam Scott]], [[Anthony Azizi]], [[Jim O'Heir]] and [[Kristen Ariza]]).

Her film work includes supporting roles in {{wt|Strangers in Paradise (1984 film)|Strangers in Paradise}} (1984), the comedy ''The Malibu Bikini Shop'' (1986, with [[Bruce Greenwood]], [[Jay Robinson]], and [[Charlie Brill]]), the music drama ''Dance Academy'' (1988, with [[Michelle Rudy]], [[Laura Feder Behr]] and [[Julie Newmar]]), {{wt|RoboCop 2}} (1990, with [[Peter Weller]], [[Roger Aaron Brown]], [[John Glover]], [[Gabriel Damon]], [[Mark Rolston]], [[Jeff McCarthy]], [[Erik Cord]], [[Stephen Lee]], [[Tzi Ma]], and [[Bill Bolender]]), {{wt|Point Break}} (1991, with [[Lori Petty]], [[Christopher Pettiet]], [[Mike Genovese]], [[Jack Kehler]], [[Raymond Forchion]], [[Jeff Imada]], and [[Curt Truman]]), and {{wt|Storyville (film)|Storyville}} (1992).

Görg later worked as producer on her father Alan Görg's projects, including the drama ''Earth Spirit'' (2006), the short drama ''Techqua Ikachi: Aboriginal Warning'' (2008), and the music comedy ''Hollywood Love'' (2011).

Görg died from cancer the day before her 56th birthday. {{el|heavy.com/entertainment/2020/07/galyn-gorg-dead/}}

