'''Mark Barrett''' is an actor who portrayed [[Lonzo]] in the {{s|DS9}} [[DS9 Season 3|third season]] episode {{e|Facets}}. His costume was sold off on the [[It's A Wrap! sale and auction]] on eBay and was previously worn by guest actor [[Lee Arenberg]] in the [[DS9 Season 1|first season]] episode {{e|The Nagus}}. {{stala|4964}}

Barrett studied acting at the American Conservatory Theater in San Francisco and earned a BA in Theater from UCLA. He is also trained in jazz and tap dance. Beside several stage plays, Barrett had featured and recurring parts in several television series, such as ''Generations'', ''General Hospital'', {{wt|Stand by Your Man (TV series)|Stand by Your Man}}, {{wt|Boy Meets World}} (starring [[William Daniels]]), {{wt|Ask Harriet}} (1998, with [[Willie Garson]] and [[Rob LaBelle]]), {{wt|The Naked Truth (TV series)|The Naked Truth}} (1998, starring [[Amy Hill]]), {{wt|Malibu, CA (TV series)|Malibu, CA}} (1999), and ''Passions''.

Among his feature film credits are {{wt|Tap (film)|Tap}} (1989, with [[Joe Morton]], [[Terrence E. McNally]] and [[Lloyd Kino]]), {{wt|Postcards from the Edge (film)|Postcards from the Edge}} (1990, with [[George D. Wallace]], [[Marcelo Tubert]], and [[Natalia Nogulich]]), {{wt|Fearless (1993 film)|Fearless}} (1993, with [[John de Lancie]], [[Steven Culp]], [[Stephanie Erb]], [[Eric Menyuk]], [[David Carpenter]], and [[Rico E. Anderson]]), the action drama ''Texas Payback'' (1998, with [[Angelo Tiffe]]), and {{wt|Scary Movie 2}} (2001, with [[Woody Bosco]], [[Drew Renkewitz]], [[Suzanne Bianqui]], [[Antony Acker]], [[LaFaye Baker]], [[Tim Rigby]], [[Bridgett Riley]] and [[Geneviere Anderson]]).

Between 2007 and 2019, Barrett worked as stand-in for actor {{w|Johnny Galecki}} on ''[[The Big Bang Theory]]''. During these twelve years he also appeared several times as background actor, mostly as an university cafeteria patron.

